  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The equivalent resistance between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> of the network shown in figure:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f1d535d5-6c3f-42fd-8e28-afd32829a589-9896252.PNG\" style=\"width: 425px; height: 150px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LXE8Q",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fGor0",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EzdVr",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nGTpA",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The given circuit can be redrawn as shown below:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b1bf5b6f-65e7-45ff-b985-a3f8cfb03a29-9896252_1.PNG\" style=\"width: 251px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>Since the circuit is in balanced wheatstone configuration,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistor&nbsp;can be omitted. Now, the circuit has two branches having two resistors connected in series.&nbsp;</p><p>Therefore, the resistance of upper branch is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and lower branch is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi></math>.</p><p>The equivalent resistance will therefore be:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
